From 96745cc967bb72e0909d971cf66a487249d0cd7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Martin <rob@version2beta.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:04:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] task(T-A010): chunkedreader: unblock parallel reader on
 worker failure or cancellation (backport)

Backport of rclone/rclone#10172 (head eaadb88cd150), carried as
webui/backports/03-pr10172.patch until upstream merges it.

Upstream commit message:

chunkedreader: unblock parallel reader on worker failure or cancellation

In chunkedreader/parallel, background worker goroutines fetch chunk buffers
while stream.read waits on s.rw.WaitWrite holding the reader mutex cr.mu.

If a worker goroutine encountered a connection failure, premature EOF, or
cancellation, it recorded the error on s.err and terminated. However,
consumers in stream.read continued waiting indefinitely for missing bytes
from s.rw because no mechanism signaled worker termination.

Furthermore, calling parallel.Close() blocked trying to acquire cr.mu,
which was held by the hung Read() call, resulting in an unrecoverable deadlock.

Fix this by:
1. Replacing s.err chan error with a close-signaling s.done channel that
   reliably wakes waiting consumers on any worker exit.
2. Adding a cancel context to parallel that cancels in-flight reader waits
   before Close acquires cr.mu.
3. Adding TestParallelProducerFailure covering open failure, short read EOF,
   and mid-stream connection loss.

PEV-Plan: 001_plan-WebdavSuperUI
PEV-Unit: T-A010
PEV-Attempt: 1
PEV-Result: pass
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
